---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="alert-notify Documentation: Quick start"
  description="Show your first alert-notify toast in minutes: install, call toast.success, then set optional global defaults with toast.config."
  pageTitle="Quick start"
>
  <p>
    Get a working toast with the core API. This path works in any JavaScript app. Framework helpers are optional.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Install</h2>
  <pre class="api"><code>{`npm install alert-notify`}</code></pre>

  <h2>2. Call toast</h2>
  <pre class="api"><code>{`import { toast } from "alert-notify";

toast.success("Your profile was saved.", { title: "Profile updated" });
toast.error("Please try again.", { title: "Something went wrong" });
toast.promise(save(), {
  loading: "Saving…",
  success: "Saved",
  error: (err) => (err instanceof Error ? err.message : "Failed"),
});`}</code></pre>

  <h2>3. Optional defaults</h2>
  <pre class="api"><code>{`toast.config({
  position: "top-right",
  theme: "light",
  richColors: true,
});`}</code></pre>

  <p>
    Next, pick a stack guide under Choose integration, or open the
    <a href="/examples">playground</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
